es/75/75f479ff700f106f5cae6bafa94df87381d5fc0fca1758aad55f6bc5be1d7c38.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following is the graph of $y=f(\\frac{1}{4}x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "To graph the function $y=f(\\frac{1}{4}x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and stretch it by factor of $4$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $4.$\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/0f/0f3cf395fe5f442212e057f73ef48ab458370e914424e186611c70f1c9f29953.png)"} :step/id #uuid "2fd6cb82-b73f-5f34-aa6e-4be98186d7a6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548129}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548124 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a3c7b4e-4a32-5c4b-a2b0-8a1ec78a4aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/98/98794731402303a4a3ecf117f3e7b8ec63eb4a43cb10ee18b3c366aefcc6aaba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547370} {:answer/id #uuid "2c930ef4-0f0c-547e-a098-8e05ad168b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c1/c1620eef61866616e0c391269285d545672d423430789e6412f64ef79f5a8397.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547405} {:answer/id #uuid "2cba8113-a2f6-54aa-bcc3-ce7a178f9605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/75/75c30e74e1c90de6fcf76dfcc88968178049c796b7c21bc40eaad29e81dc6a49.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547406} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb8665f-6599-50d0-940b-9c7bb36da2f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d5/d50065e4fea4e110bac262b0734cb670e9c5a6e8e5538c6e91248f7fbe5ca40d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547728} {:answer/id #uuid "ceeef5b0-fdd7-58ba-94f7-3a65f57a0f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ef/ef009197f1b86d68aca70289966e769f03cdd498f92635009511da38061f7549.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547760}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547760} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c44bb2-3c0d-5864-a1e0-28e654b1d9c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "28d08449-f19d-5dae-9ff9-1b1d3bcb8500" :question/math-academy-id "q-17605" :question/problem "![](images/a6/a66ac2663dadacc0648b5a8993df40edafe8c7c2ee9dddac4ef932203b99dbd7.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following is the graph of $y=f(\\frac{1}{4}x)?$" :question/worked-solution "To graph the function $y=f(\\frac{1}{4}x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and stretch it by factor of $4$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $4.$\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/f5/f5de147e69639b8cfbbe591241603d437650b88d523058df09dd30b60a6482da.png)"} :step/id #uuid "7de9a451-20cb-530d-be6d-f500ce4d71dc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548094}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548129 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c7ef0e-ae5f-5788-8442-58796873f024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-2,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547526} {:answer/id #uuid "84e944cf-269e-5563-8b06-449f37d3b2c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-6,27)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547601} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ab2f07-2154-5eaf-9f99-57f63be7b49d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-18,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547705} {:answer/id #uuid "d0e15f87-be8f-5c3b-8a1b-1ee813c884df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-6,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547764} {:answer/id #uuid "e91d2864-f866-5e4b-b852-31fa590ce52f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547801}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547705} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dc935dc-f462-5bbc-b210-6779d4c833a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7ec57449-f520-50b3-b823-1f98b4f880f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-79428" :question/problem "The point $P$ with coordinates $(-6,9)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(\\frac{1}{3}x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $y=f(\\frac{1}{3}x)$ represents a stretch of the function $y=f(x)$ by a factor of $3$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-6,9)$ on $f(x)$ is mapped to the point $(3\\cdot (-6),9)=(-18,9),$ and this point must lie on the graph of $y=f(\\frac{1}{3}x)$"} :step/id #uuid "88584094-7c93-5f8c-acd3-2211dd446362"}] :activity/title "Horizontal Stretches of Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547302}]}
